This essay originally appeared in  The Guardian . It&#8217;s an expanded version of the one I posted as &#8220; We Get the Infrastructure We Pay For .&#8221;  
 It&#8217;s been a bad week for our computerized infrastructure. We&#8217;ve seen outages at  Microsoft , the  FAA , a handful of  banks ,  United Airlines , an unnamed classified  NSA network , and  Apple . People should be forgiven for suspecting a coordinated cyberattack, a common cause, or at least a conspiracy. But there is none. 
